```

Two notes on choices I made while writing the plan:

- The three `DeliveryNotes.kt` blocks are one logical change split into three anchors so each SEARCH stays short and unique: the constants/regex/compose block after the data class, the added KDoc paragraph at the end of the existing KDoc, and the strict branch at the top of the `for (line in lines)` loop, using the design's `?.let { ... continue }` shape.
- In the tests, `normalisedField` implements N(U) exactly as the design defines it, and the fixtures list includes `null` plus the three note strings from `DeliveryNotesParserTest.kt`, so the Theorem B fixture test covers the empty case too (`compose(parse(null))` is `""` and `parse("")` equals the all-null sections).
